[{"code":"program_shape","severity":"error","span":{"file":"src/Main.beni","start":{"line":31,"col":72},"end":{"line":31,"col":77}},"title":"PROGRAM SHAPE","message":"The page's value is read here, outside the record's `init`: only `init` may read\nit. Put it in the model in `init`, `init = λ⊤ → ( { page = page }, Cmd.none )`,\nand read `model.page` in `view` and `update`. A limit of the compiler, not a\nrule: `view`, `update` and `subscriptions` are compiled as functions of the\nmodel, whose writes the compiler tracks, and the value is not in the model until\n`init` puts it there (`docs/design/prerender.md` §8.4;\n`docs/design/browser-inline.md` §5, class 4)."}]
